#: ../../docstring deserialize.DeserializerAssetsStandard:3 of
msgid ""
"**A divergence absorbed here:** the Python signature accepts two "
"arbitrary *callables*, and author modules really do use that — something "
"along the lines of \"treat a dash as zero, otherwise parse an integer\". "
"The bridge does not try to guess which built-in function a callable "
"corresponds to: it calls it, through `num_converter_of` and "
"`date_converter_of`, which is the only translation that loses no "
"behaviour."
msgstr ""

